    {
      "name": "getSecureCredentials",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "options",
          "type": {
            "k": "ref",
            "name": "GetSecureCredentialsOptions"
          },
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "k": "ref",
        "name": "Credentials"
      },
      "promise": true,
      "comment": "Gets the stored credentials for a given server, requiring biometric authentication.\nCredentials must have been stored with accessControl set to BIOMETRY_CURRENT_SET or BIOMETRY_ANY.\n\nOn iOS, the system automatically shows the biometric prompt when accessing the protected Keychain item.\nOn Android, BiometricPrompt is shown with a CryptoObject bound to the credential decryption key.\n\nIf no protected credentials exist for the server, the promise rejects with code `21`\n(`BiometricAuthError.NO_PROTECTED_CREDENTIALS_FOUND`). This is stable, expected\nbehavior — for example when credentials were never saved with biometric protection,\nwere deleted, or were invalidated after biometric enrollment changes.\n`isCredentialsSaved()` returns true when any credentials (protected or unprotected) exist,\nso it does not guarantee a biometric-protected entry is present — handle code `21` in\nyour catch block or only call after storing with `accessControl` BIOMETRY_CURRENT_SET\nor BIOMETRY_ANY.\nPlatform messages: Android `No protected credentials found`, iOS\n`No protected credentials found for server`."
    },
    {
      "name": "isCredentialsSaved",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "options",
          "type": {
            "k": "ref",
            "name": "IsCredentialsSavedOptions"
          },
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "k": "ref",
        "name": "IsCredentialsSavedResult"
      },
      "promise": true,
      "comment": "Checks if credentials are already saved for a given server."
    },
    {
      "name": "setData",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "options",
          "type": {
            "k": "ref",
            "name": "SetDataOptions"
          },
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "k": "unit"
      },
      "promise": true,
      "comment": "Stores an arbitrary string value under the given key.\nValues are encrypted at rest using the platform secure storage backend\n(Android Keystore + SharedPreferences, iOS Keychain).\n\nFor biometric-protected storage, set `accessControl` and retrieve the value\nwith `getSecureData()`. Credential helpers remain available for username/password flows."
    },
    {
      "name": "getData",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "options",
          "type": {
            "k": "ref",
            "name": "GetDataOptions"
          },
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "k": "ref",
        "name": "StoredData"
      },
      "promise": true,
      "comment": "Gets a previously stored value for the given key.\nOnly returns values stored without biometric `accessControl`."
    },
    {
      "name": "getSecureData",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "options",
